 "result_text": "I fixed the bug in `wcmatch/glob.py`. `glob([\"dummy\", \"**/this_script.py\"])` should now find `this_script.py` as `glob([\"**/this_script.py\", \"dummy\"])` does. I haven't run your example or the test suite.\n\nAs the issue said, `curdir` was set once before the loop over patterns. A non-magic pattern like `\"dummy\"` overwrote it with its own starting directory. Any magic pattern after it then globbed from that directory instead of the current one, which is why the result came back empty.\n\nThe fix moves `curdir = self.current` inside the loop, so each pattern starts from the current directory.\n\nI didn't add or change any tests, and I haven't committed.",
